Dimensionality-reduction pipelines write each fit as one `.npz` file instead of a folder of files, and a nested reducer's sweep (PCA fitted once at its largest dimension) as one file holding every dimension, read with `load_fit_artifact(path, n_components=...)` or `slice_fit_artifact`. No file is written per evaluation: `run_eval` returns the evaluation's inventory record, which is its only copy. A large grid uses about ten times fewer files, and PCA sweeps store their embedding once instead of once per dimension. Fit files no longer keep a copy of their score payload and summary. Run folders written in the old layout are fitted again on resume.
